Part B is built and logged. The one critic round scored it **7.6 on the benchmark rubric** (target 9.2) and **7.9 on the studio rubric**, a fail by 0.1. I fixed both score caps and 12 more issues after that round, but nothing has been re-scored.

**Simulated backend**
- The full mock catalogue now drives the backend: 24 cities, 12 airlines each with its own fare families, and 96 hotels with rate plans, reviews and guest scores.
- Every existing id, route and export name still works, so Developer A's homepage picks up the new data.
- Hotel photos come from a pool of this design's own photos. No two hotels in a city share a lead photo, and neighbouring results never repeat one in any sort.

**Pages built (P1)**
- **Flight results:** date and price strip, Best / Cheapest / Fastest tabs, 10 filter groups with counts, all kept in the URL.
